After thorough analysis of issue #462 requesting that wardrobe collection removal should "go through the items in the collection, and if they are still there, clear the slot for them," I found that this functionality is **already correctly implemented** in the existing codebase.

## Current Implementation

The `UnloadWardrobeCollection` method in `DynamicCharacterAvatar.cs` (lines 2075-2099) already handles the requirement:

```csharp
public void UnloadWardrobeCollection(string collectionToUnload)
{
    foreach (KeyValuePair<string, UMAWardrobeCollection> kp in _wardrobeCollections)
    {
        if (kp.Value.name == collectionToUnload)
        {
            var wardrobeSet = kp.Value.GetRacesWardrobeSet(activeRace.racedata);
            if (wardrobeSet.Count > 0)
            {
                for (int si = 0; si < wardrobeSet.Count; si++)
                {
                    if (_wardrobeRecipes.ContainsKey(wardrobeSet[si].slot))
                    {
                        if (_wardrobeRecipes[wardrobeSet[si].slot].name == wardrobeSet[si].recipe)
                        {
                            ClearSlot(wardrobeSet[si].slot);
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
            _wardrobeCollections.Remove(kp.Value.wardrobeSlot);
            break;
        }
    }
}
```

## Key Features

✅ **Goes through items in collection**: Uses `GetRacesWardrobeSet()` to iterate through all wardrobe items for the current race  
✅ **Checks if they are still there**: Verifies the slot contains a recipe AND it's the exact same recipe from the collection  
✅ **Clears the slot**: Calls `ClearSlot()` only for items that match the original collection items  

## Smart Behavior

The implementation preserves user customization - if a user loads a collection then manually changes one of the slots to a different recipe, unloading the collection will NOT remove that manually changed item, only the unchanged collection items.

